  "problem": "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=⟨{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y,\\,{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y⟩$ and the points $O(0,0)$ and $A(1,\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ in the $xy$-plane. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $F$ is conservative.\n- ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=e,$ where ${C}_{1}$ is the path along the line segment $\\overset{―}{OA},$ traversed from $O$ to $A.$\n- ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=2e-1,$ where ${C}_{2}$ is the path along the curve $y=\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\sqrt{x},$ traversed from $O$ to $A.$",
